{%- comment -%}
  ElmsNest PDP — טבלת השוואה (v2).

  v1 was a bare 13px table on the cream ground: correct, and invisible. v2 keeps
  the real <table> — one <th scope="row"> per criterion, one <th scope="col"> per
  side — and gives it weight on the night ground, where the amber accent is the
  colour of the light the products emit.

  The ElmsNest column is the hero and says so structurally, not by adjective:
  an amber cap rule, an amber crest, an amber column name and a lifted amber
  wash that runs unbroken from the header down through the last row. The
  comparison column stays plain — it is not attacked, it is simply not lit.

  Marks are never colour alone. Every mark renders a distinct glyph shape
  (✓ / ✗ / –) plus a word: the merchant's own text when they wrote one, and the
  Hebrew state word otherwise, so the meaning survives greyscale, colour-blind
  vision and a screen reader with images off.

  The comparison column defaults deliberately say "משתנה" rather than asserting a
  failure of unnamed competitors: the store cannot verify what an arbitrary
  generic lamp does. Every cell is a schema setting, so any sharper claim is the
  merchant's own and made knowingly. Nothing here is an invented spec, rating or
  count — the section renders only what the merchant typed.

  Every direction-dependent CSS property is logical — the store is Hebrew RTL.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign elms_row_count = 0
  for block in section.blocks
    if block.settings.criterion != blank
      assign elms_row_count = elms_row_count | plus: 1
    endif
  endfor

  assign elms_ground = section.settings.ground | default: 'night'
  assign elms_crest = section.settings.crest_icon | default: 'sun'
  assign elms_sides = 'a,b' | split: ','
-%}

{%- if section.settings.enable and elms_row_count > 0 -%}
  <section
    class="elms-pdp elms-compare elms-compare--{{ elms_ground }}"
    dir="rtl"
    {% if section.settings.heading != blank %}
      aria-labelledby="elms-compare-title-{{ section.id }}"
    {% else %}
      aria-label="השוואה"
    {% endif %}
    style="--elms-compare-pt: {{ section.settings.padding_top }}px; --elms-compare-pb: {{ section.settings.padding_bottom }}px;{% if elms_ground == 'custom' %} --elms-compare-bg: {{ section.settings.bg_color }}; --elms-compare-fg: {{ section.settings.text_color }}; --elms-compare-soft: {{ section.settings.text_color | color_mix: section.settings.bg_color, 70 }}; --elms-compare-faint: {{ section.settings.text_color | color_mix: section.settings.bg_color, 52 }}; --elms-compare-line: {{ section.settings.text_color | color_mix: section.settings.bg_color, 16 }}; --elms-compare-kicker: {{ section.settings.text_color | color_mix: section.settings.bg_color, 70 }}; --elms-compare-accent: {{ section.settings.text_color }}; --elms-compare-accent-text: {{ section.settings.text_color }}; --elms-compare-hero-bg: {{ section.settings.text_color | color_mix: section.settings.bg_color, 5 }}; --elms-compare-hero-head: {{ section.settings.text_color | color_mix: section.settings.bg_color, 10 }}; --elms-compare-hero-line: {{ section.settings.text_color | color_mix: section.settings.bg_color, 24 }}; --elms-compare-focus: {{ section.settings.text_color }};{% endif %}"
  >
    <div class="elms-compare__wrap">
      {%- if section.settings.kicker != blank or section.settings.heading != blank or section.settings.subheading != blank -%}
        <header class="elms-compare__header">
          {%- if section.settings.kicker != blank -%}
            <p class="elms-compare__kicker">{{ section.settings.kicker }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
            <h2 class="elms-compare__title" id="elms-compare-title-{{ section.id }}">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h2>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if section.settings.subheading != blank -%}
            <p class="elms-compare__sub">{{ section.settings.subheading }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
        </header>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        Measured, not assumed: an overflow-x container with a min-inline-size
        does NOT contain itself in RTL. At a 375px viewport Chromium reported
        document.documentElement.scrollWidth = 446 against a 375px client width,
        i.e. the page itself gained a horizontal scrollbar. So below 760px the
        table stacks into one card per row instead of scrolling.

        The stack is a display change only. Every element keeps an explicit ARIA
        role, because a <table> that is display:block loses its implicit table
        role in Chromium and Firefox — with the roles declared the table
        semantics survive the restyle. The <thead> goes away at that width, so
        every cell also carries its own column name.

        The overflow-x container stays as a floor for the widths where the table
        does render as a table and a merchant has typed an unusually long row.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="elms-compare__scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="טבלת השוואה">
        <table class="elms-compare__table" role="table">
          <thead role="rowgroup">
            <tr role="row">
              <th scope="col" role="columnheader" class="elms-compare__th elms-compare__th--criterion">
                {{ section.settings.criterion_label }}
              </th>

              <th scope="col" role="columnheader" class="elms-compare__th elms-compare__th--a">
                <span class="elms-compare__crest">
                  {%- render 'elms-pdp-icon', name: elms_crest -%}
                </span>
                <span class="elms-compare__col-name"><bdi dir="auto">{{ section.settings.col_a_label }}</bdi></span>
              </th>

              <th scope="col" role="columnheader" class="elms-compare__th elms-compare__th--b">
                <span class="elms-compare__col-name"><bdi dir="auto">{{ section.settings.col_b_label }}</bdi></span>
              </th>
            </tr>
          </thead>

          <tbody role="rowgroup">
            {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
              {%- if block.settings.criterion != blank -%}
                <tr role="row" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                  <th scope="row" role="rowheader" class="elms-compare__criterion">{{ block.settings.criterion }}</th>

                  {%- for elms_side in elms_sides -%}
                    {%- liquid
                      if elms_side == 'a'
                        assign elms_mark = block.settings.mark_a | default: 'none'
                        assign elms_text = block.settings.text_a
                        assign elms_col_name = section.settings.col_a_label
                      else
                        assign elms_mark = block.settings.mark_b | default: 'none'
                        assign elms_text = block.settings.text_b
                        assign elms_col_name = section.settings.col_b_label
                      endif

                      case elms_mark
                        when 'check'
                          assign elms_word = 'יש'
                        when 'cross'
                          assign elms_word = 'אין'
                        when 'partial'
                          assign elms_word = 'חלקי'
                        else
                          assign elms_word = 'לא צוין'
                      endcase
                    -%}
                    <td role="cell" class="elms-compare__cell elms-compare__cell--{{ elms_side }}">
                      {%- comment -%}
                        Hidden while the <thead> is visible, shown once the row
                        becomes a card and the column headers are gone.
                      {%- endcomment -%}
                      <span class="elms-compare__cell-label"><bdi dir="auto">{{ elms_col_name }}</bdi></span>

                      <span class="elms-compare__mark elms-compare__mark--{{ elms_mark }}">
                        {%- case elms_mark -%}
                          {%- when 'check' -%}
                            <span class="elms-compare__glyph" aria-hidden="true">
                              {%- render 'elms-pdp-icon', name: 'check' -%}
                            </span>
                          {%- when 'cross' -%}
                            <span class="elms-compare__glyph" aria-hidden="true">
                              {%- render 'elms-pdp-icon', name: 'cross' -%}
                            </span>
                          {%- when 'partial' -%}
                            <span class="elms-compare__glyph" aria-hidden="true">–</span>
                        {%- endcase -%}

                        <span class="elms-compare__mark-text">
                          {%- if elms_text != blank -%}
                            {%- unless elms_mark == 'none' -%}
                              <span class="elms-compare__sr">{{ elms_word }}. </span>
                            {%- endunless -%}
                            <bdi dir="auto">{{ elms_text }}</bdi>
                          {%- else -%}
                            {{ elms_word }}
                          {%- endif -%}
                        </span>
                      </span>
                    </td>
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </tr>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        The rule belongs to the band and spans it; the note's measure does not,
        so the two live on separate elements.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if section.settings.note != blank -%}
        <div class="elms-compare__foot">
          <p class="elms-compare__note">{{ section.settings.note }}</p>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </section>
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  .elms-compare,
  .elms-compare * { box-sizing: border-box; }

  .elms-compare {
    direction: rtl;
    background: var(--elms-compare-bg);
    color: var(--elms-compare-fg);
    padding-block-start: var(--elms-compare-pt);
    padding-block-end: var(--elms-compare-pb);
    padding-inline: clamp(16px, 3vw, 32px);
  }

  /* --- Grounds ---------------------------------------------------------
     Night is the default: the amber accent only means "light" against a dark
     ground. On cream, amber on paper is a 1.8:1 text contrast, so the accent
     role falls back to the ink tokens and amber is simply not used. */

  .elms-compare--night {
    --elms-compare-bg: rgb(var(--en-night));
    --elms-compare-fg: rgb(var(--en-ink));
    --elms-compare-soft: rgb(var(--en-ink) / .68);
    --elms-compare-faint: rgb(var(--en-ink) / .52);
    --elms-compare-line: rgb(var(--en-ink) / .14);
    --elms-compare-kicker: rgb(var(--en-amber));
    --elms-compare-accent: rgb(var(--en-amber));
    --elms-compare-accent-text: rgb(var(--en-amber-soft));
    --elms-compare-hero-bg: rgb(var(--en-amber) / .08);
    --elms-compare-hero-head: rgb(var(--en-amber) / .15);
    --elms-compare-hero-line: rgb(var(--en-amber) / .32);
    --elms-compare-focus: rgb(var(--en-focus-dark));
  }

  .elms-compare--cream {
    --elms-compare-bg: rgb(var(--en-surface-page));
    --elms-compare-fg: rgb(var(--en-text-primary));
    --elms-compare-soft: rgb(var(--en-text-secondary));
    --elms-compare-faint: rgb(var(--en-text-muted));
    --elms-compare-line: rgb(var(--en-border-subtle));
    --elms-compare-kicker: rgb(var(--en-text-muted));
    --elms-compare-accent: rgb(var(--en-text-primary));
    --elms-compare-accent-text: rgb(var(--en-text-primary));
    --elms-compare-hero-bg: rgb(var(--en-text-primary) / .05);
    --elms-compare-hero-head: rgb(var(--en-text-primary) / .09);
    --elms-compare-hero-line: rgb(var(--en-text-primary) / .22);
    --elms-compare-focus: rgb(var(--en-focus-light));
  }

  /* The custom ground reads every colour from the merchant's two colour
     settings, injected on the section element itself. */

  .elms-compare__wrap {
    inline-size: min(1180px, 100%);
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  /* --- Band header. Title:body is 46:16 = 2.9x at 1440px. -------------- */

  /* Measure lives on the title and the sub in `em`, never on the header in
     `ch`. `ch` resolves against the containing block's font-size, not the
     heading's: 58ch on this header measured 500.25px at a 1440px viewport
     inside a 1180px wrap, i.e. it squeezed the 46px title into a ribbon.
     `em` scales with each element's own size, so the limit follows the type. */
  .elms-compare__header {
    margin-block-end: clamp(32px, 4vw, 56px);
  }

  .elms-compare__kicker {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.4;
    letter-spacing: .10em;
    color: var(--elms-compare-kicker);
  }

  .elms-compare__kicker::after {
    content: "";
    display: block;
    inline-size: 40px;
    block-size: 2px;
    margin-block-start: 12px;
    background: var(--elms-compare-kicker);
  }

  /* The theme sets its own h2 colour, which beats plain inheritance from the
     section root — so the title states its ground colour explicitly. */
  .elms-compare__title {
    max-inline-size: 14em;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--elms-compare-fg);
    font-size: clamp(30px, 3.6vw, 46px);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.14;
    letter-spacing: -.01em;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .elms-compare__sub {
    max-inline-size: 32em;
    margin: 16px 0 0;
    font-size: clamp(16px, 1.3vw, 19px);
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--elms-compare-soft);
    text-align: start;
  }

  /* --- Table shell ------------------------------------------------------ */

  .elms-compare__scroll {
    overflow-x: auto;
    -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;
    border: 1px solid var(--elms-compare-line);
  }

  .elms-compare__scroll:focus-visible {
    outline: 3px solid var(--elms-compare-focus);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }

  /* --- Table ----------------------------------------------------------- */

  .elms-compare__table {
    inline-size: 100%;
    min-inline-size: 600px;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 16px;
  }

  .elms-compare__table th,
  .elms-compare__table td {
    padding-block: 18px;
    padding-inline: clamp(14px, 1.6vw, 22px);
    text-align: start;
    vertical-align: top;
    line-height: 1.6;
    border-block-end: 1px solid var(--elms-compare-line);
  }

  .elms-compare__table thead th {
    vertical-align: bottom;
    padding-block-start: clamp(20px, 2.4vw, 30px);
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  .elms-compare__th--criterion {
    inline-size: 40%;
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.4;
    letter-spacing: .10em;
    color: var(--elms-compare-faint);
  }

  .elms-compare__th--a,
  .elms-compare__th--b { inline-size: 30%; }

  /* The hero column: an amber cap rule, an amber wash and amber hairlines
     that run unbroken from this cell down to the last row. */
  .elms-compare__th--a {
    background: var(--elms-compare-hero-head);
    border-block-start: 3px solid var(--elms-compare-accent);
    border-inline: 1px solid var(--elms-compare-hero-line);
  }

  .elms-compare__crest {
    display: block;
    inline-size: 44px;
    block-size: 44px;
    margin-block-end: 14px;
    color: var(--elms-compare-accent);
  }

  .elms-compare__crest svg {
    display: block;
    inline-size: 100%;
    block-size: 100%;
  }

  .elms-compare__col-name {
    display: block;
    font-size: clamp(20px, 1.9vw, 24px);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.25;
    letter-spacing: -.01em;
  }

  .elms-compare__th--a .elms-compare__col-name { color: var(--elms-compare-accent-text); }
  .elms-compare__th--b .elms-compare__col-name { color: var(--elms-compare-soft); }

  .elms-compare__criterion {
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--elms-compare-fg);
  }

  .elms-compare__cell--a {
    background: var(--elms-compare-hero-bg);
    border-inline: 1px solid var(--elms-compare-hero-line);
    color: var(--elms-compare-fg);
  }

  .elms-compare__cell--b { color: var(--elms-compare-soft); }

  /* The column name repeated inside every cell — dead weight while the real
     column headers are on screen, so it only exists in the stacked layout. */
  .elms-compare__cell-label { display: none; }

  /* Scoped to the widths that actually render a table, so the stacked layout
     below does not have to out-specify these. */
  @media (min-width: 761px) {
    .elms-compare__table tbody tr:last-child th,
    .elms-compare__table tbody tr:last-child td { border-block-end: 0; }

    /* The hero wash needs a floor, or the column bleeds into the frame. */
    .elms-compare__table tbody tr:last-child .elms-compare__cell--a {
      border-block-end: 1px solid var(--elms-compare-hero-line);
    }
  }

  /* --- Marks. Shape + word first, colour last. -------------------------- */

  .elms-compare__mark {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .elms-compare__glyph {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    inline-size: 26px;
    block-size: 26px;
    margin-block-start: 1px;
    border: 1px solid currentColor;
    color: var(--elms-compare-faint);
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .elms-compare__glyph svg {
    display: block;
    inline-size: 18px;
    block-size: 18px;
  }

  .elms-compare__cell--a .elms-compare__mark--check .elms-compare__glyph {
    background: var(--elms-compare-hero-head);
    color: var(--elms-compare-accent);
  }

  .elms-compare__mark-text {
    min-inline-size: 0;
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    overflow-wrap: break-word;
  }

  .elms-compare__sr {
    position: absolute;
    inline-size: 1px;
    block-size: 1px;
    padding: 0;
    margin: -1px;
    overflow: hidden;
    clip-path: inset(50%);
    white-space: nowrap;
    border: 0;
  }

  .elms-compare__foot {
    margin-block-start: clamp(28px, 3vw, 40px);
    padding-block-start: 18px;
    border-block-start: 1px solid var(--elms-compare-line);
  }

  .elms-compare__note {
    max-inline-size: 42em;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--elms-compare-soft);
    text-align: start;
  }

  /* --- Stacked cards. One card per criterion, hero panel first. ---------
     Three columns at 360px leave roughly 100px per value, so below 760px the
     rows stack instead of scrolling. This is a display change only — the ARIA
     roles in the markup keep the table semantics through it. */

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .elms-compare {
      padding-block-start: calc(var(--elms-compare-pt) * .62);
      padding-block-end: calc(var(--elms-compare-pb) * .62);
    }

    .elms-compare__scroll { border: 0; }

    .elms-compare__table {
      display: block;
      min-inline-size: 0;
    }

    /* The hero column header survives the stack as a banner rather than being
       hidden with the rest of the <thead>: it carries the 44px crest, which is
       the band's largest visual, and hiding the whole thead took the band's
       only >=40px asset with it (measured 0x0 below 761px). The criterion and
       comparison headers still go — every cell carries its own column name. */
    .elms-compare__table thead,
    .elms-compare__table thead tr { display: block; }

    .elms-compare__table .elms-compare__th--criterion,
    .elms-compare__table .elms-compare__th--b { display: none; }

    .elms-compare__table .elms-compare__th--a {
      inline-size: auto;
      border-inline: 0;
      border-block-end: 1px solid var(--elms-compare-hero-line);
      margin-block-end: 14px;
    }

    .elms-compare__table tbody { display: block; }

    .elms-compare__table tbody tr {
      display: block;
      border: 1px solid var(--elms-compare-line);
    }

    .elms-compare__table tbody tr + tr { margin-block-start: 14px; }

    .elms-compare__table th,
    .elms-compare__table td {
      display: block;
      padding-block: 15px;
      padding-inline: 16px;
      border-block-end: 0;
    }

    .elms-compare__table .elms-compare__criterion {
      border-block-end: 1px solid var(--elms-compare-line);
    }

    /* The hero panel keeps its wash and takes an amber bar on the leading edge
       in place of the two hairlines it had as a column. */
    .elms-compare__table .elms-compare__cell--a {
      border-inline: 0;
      border-inline-start: 3px solid var(--elms-compare-accent);
      border-block-end: 1px solid var(--elms-compare-line);
    }

    .elms-compare__cell-label {
      display: block;
      margin-block-end: 8px;
      font-size: 13px;
      font-weight: 600;
      line-height: 1.4;
      letter-spacing: .10em;
    }

    .elms-compare__cell--a .elms-compare__cell-label { color: var(--elms-compare-accent-text); }
    .elms-compare__cell--b .elms-compare__cell-label { color: var(--elms-compare-faint); }

    .elms-compare__mark { gap: 10px; }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "PDP · טבלת השוואה",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "elms-pdp-section",
  "max_blocks": 8,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "enable",
      "label": "הצגת המקטע",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "kicker",
      "label": "שורת פתיחה קצרה",
      "info": "מופיעה מעל הכותרת בצבע ההדגשה. השאירו ריק כדי להסתיר.",
      "default": "השוואה"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "כותרת המקטע",
      "default": "מה ההבדל מול מנורה סולארית זולה"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "subheading",
      "label": "שורת משנה",
      "default": "ההשוואה מתייחסת לאופן שבו אנחנו מוכרים — לא להבטחת ביצועים של מוצר מסוים."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "note",
      "label": "הערה בתחתית המקטע",
      "default": "אנחנו לא מתחייבים על ביצועי מוצרים של מוכרים אחרים. הטבלה מתארת את מה שאנחנו מפרסמים בעמוד המוצר שלנו."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "כותרות העמודות"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "criterion_label",
      "label": "כותרת עמודת הקריטריון",
      "default": "מה בודקים"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "col_a_label",
      "label": "כותרת העמודה שלנו",
      "default": "ElmsNest"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "col_b_label",
      "label": "כותרת עמודת ההשוואה",
      "default": "מנורה גנרית זולה"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "crest_icon",
      "label": "סמל העמודה שלנו",
      "info": "מופיע מעל שם העמודה שלנו, בצבע ההדגשה.",
      "options": [
        { "value": "sun", "label": "שמש — טעינה סולארית" },
        { "value": "bolt", "label": "ברק — הספק" },
        { "value": "shield", "label": "מגן — עמידות" },
